  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1005 PM CDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nA more zonal pattern will setup starting Thursday that will carry\ninto the weekend. Weak shortwaves will periodically ripple \nthrough this flow, resulting in low to medium rain and storm \nchances between 30-50% in the forecast each day through Saturday. \nAn expansive area of high pressure will move over the southeast by\nthe start of next week, bringing hot and dry conditions to Middle\nTN. Temperatures will gradually warm through the weekend as this \nfeature approaches with afternoon temperatures warming into in the\nlow 90s. By Monday, widespread low to mid 90s appear likely west \nof the Plateau. Heat index values will rise into the 100s this \nweekend and into next week, so keep this in mind if you have any \noutdoor events planned. There is good model agreement in this high\npressure influencing our weather through at least the first half \nof next week.",
